GNU findutils for OpenVMS
=========================

This is GNU findutils @VERSION@ (find and xargs) built natively for OpenVMS
@ARCH@, from the unmodified release plus the patches in the vms-findutils
project:

    https://github.com/issinoho/vms-findutils

Kit version: @KITVERSION@.  GNU findutils is free software under the GNU
General Public License, version 3 or later; see COPYING.  The manuals are
FIND.1 and XARGS.1, also as plain text in FIND.TXT and XARGS.TXT.

Files
-----
    FINDUTILS$ROOT:[BIN]FIND.EXE
    FINDUTILS$ROOT:[BIN]XARGS.EXE
    FINDUTILS$ROOT:[DOC]                          this file, COPYING, NEWS, the manuals
    FINDUTILS$ROOT:[000000]FINDUTILS$SETUP.COM    defines the find and xargs commands
    SYS$STARTUP:FINDUTILS$STARTUP.COM             defines FINDUTILS$ROOT

Setup
-----
The kit installs FINDUTILS$STARTUP.COM into SYS$STARTUP and runs it once.
To define FINDUTILS$ROOT at every boot, the system manager adds this line to
SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM:

    $ @SYS$STARTUP:FINDUTILS$STARTUP.COM

Each user then defines the commands (for example in LOGIN.COM):

    $ @FINDUTILS$ROOT:[000000]FINDUTILS$SETUP.COM

Use
---
    $ find . "-name" "*.c"            ! list C sources under the current directory

Known limits
------------
locate and updatedb are not included in this release.
